  IN THE LEARNED REGIME the compressive stage is `bias -> rate` at 0.34, against
  0.66 for the other. Over the WHOLE ladder that inverts, because the
  centroid saturates near its bound at high k -- a regime only an oracle
  reaches, and reporting one fit across both would name the wrong stage.

  SO THE TARGET IS THE NEURON, NOT THE POOLING. `bias -> rate` is the
  drive-to-rate transfer, and at the magnitudes reward can reach it is
  already sublinear -- which is why `poolbeta` sharpened the POOLING and
  bought convergence speed rather than ceiling. It was attacking the stage
  that is NOT compressive where the learned bias lives.
